[32m[2025-07-27 18:07:03,738] [    INFO][0m - ['ulti-label classification is a supervised learning technique where a single output example can belong to more than one class. This technique is useful for tasks that involve assigning multiple labels to an input example. For example, a task may require predicting all labels that describe the contents of an image such as, “sports”, “outdoors”, “indoors”. Such tasks can be solved by multi-label classification models which are made up of multiple classifiers that each handle one label. The input example is first classified by a base model that predicts the most likely labels. Subsequently, the labels which have a confidence score above a certain threshold are chosen by the model. The multi-label classification model can learn correlations between related labels and can even predict layers of labels like a taxonomy.<|eot_id|>\n\n'][0m
