[32m[2025-07-27 18:08:59,083] [    INFO][0m - ['. Preheat oven to 350 °F (175 °C). \n2. Grease a 9-inch pie dish.\n3. Peel and thinly slice apples. \n4. Place apple slices in the greased pie dish.\n5. Mix 1/2 cup white sugar, 1 teaspoon ground cinnamon, and a pinch of nutmeg in a bowl.\n6. Sprinkle the mixture over the apples.\n7. Cut butter into small cubes and spread over the apples and sugar mixture.\n8. Roll out top crust large enough to cover the pie dish.\n9. Place top crust over the apples and butter.\n10. Crimp edges and cut slits in the top.\n11. Bake in the preheated oven for 35 to 45 minutes, or until golden brown.<|eot_id|>\n\n'][0m
